hw/sh4: ze0 display engine registers, vblank and 2DG handshake (TODO M8.C1e).

With ROM image A joined (M8.C1d) the applications run, but the screen
memory (phys 0x0e700000) stayed zero.  Three things stood between the
applications and the 2D engine:

1. gdisubdrv.dll drives two register blocks, DU (phys 0xfff80000) and
   2DG (phys 0xffe80000), reached through their 29-bit aliases.  New
   device ze0-gfx (hw/sh4/ze0_gfx.c) answers both with read-back storage,
   a 60 Hz DU vblank (DSSR bit 11, DIER, DSRCR) and the 2DG display-list
   handshake: DLSAR + SCLR = 1 sets SR.TRA (list end; the list is not
   executed).  Interrupts from the OAL table at 0x88005c48: DU INTEVT
   0x3e0 (INT2 bit 0, SYSINTR 33), 2DG INTEVT 0x780 (INT2 bit 12, SYSINTR
   34).  Machine options gfx= (default on) and gfx-trace= (every access
   with the guest PC under -d unimp).

2. serial_scif.dll fn 0x0398e888 spins on SCFSR.TEND of SCIF channel 8
   (0x1fe48010, about 30M reads a minute) and starves every lower
   priority thread, the UI renderer included.  The SCIF stubs now cover
   channels 0-9 (were 0-7).

3. Navi.exe died in XGLDLL.dll 0x0310b7c2 on FLDI1 with FPSCR.PR = 1
   (STATUS_ILLEGAL_INSTRUCTION).  The firmware runs on the real SH-4A;
   board flag sh4_fldi_any_pr (set by -M ze0 only) lets FLDI0/FLDI1 load
   the single register whatever PR is.

Result: AuiApp and Navi.exe submit 2DG display lists and upload glyphs
and bitmaps to VRAM by CPU; the lists themselves still need an
interpreter (TODO M8.C1f).


